[Music]  most netflix movies don't have a 200  million dollar budget but most netflix  movies aren't the gray man why has  netflix spent so much money on this  potential franchise here's everything  you need to know about the next big  movie from the directors of avengers  endgame  the grey man is a project that had been  in development hell since 2011 before it  found its home on netflix at one point  both brad pitt and charlize theron were  reportedly in talks to appear in the  film and it wasn't until early 2020 that  the movie solidified its cast and  directors the action film is based on  the book of the same name by mark graney  and follows a former cia operative on  the run in europe who's being hunted by  his former colleague on the red carpet  for spider-man no way home in december  2021 director joe russo revealed to  variety that the gray man would be  released in the summer of 2022. at the  time the director admitted the movie  still had a lot of vfx that needed to be  worked on which would consume a lot of  time in post-production  uh i think we'll probably you know lock  picture on that sometime in like  february in april netflix confirmed that  the gray man would be available for  streaming on july 22nd 2022 the official  trailer for the film revealed that the  movie will also be available to watch in  theaters with a limited release starting  on july 15th  while netflix has been pretty  tight-lipped regarding the grey man mark  granny's source novel gives us an  indication of the film's plot we won't  spoil the ending of that novel for you  though court gentry also known as cr6  also known as the grey man is a former  cia operative much like ethan hunt and  james bond six is probably the world's  best assassin with the agency  greenlighting his kills however six  uncovers some dirty secrets within the  cia and finds himself on the run from  lloyd hansen a former cia officer who is  now employed by a shady french  organization when the president of  nigeria calls for six's murder hansen  and his allies oblige in order to  maintain a good relationship for a  lucrative oil deal it's currently  unclear if netflix's adaptation will  strictly stick to the same plot as the  novel  it was first reported that joe and  anthony russo of marvel studios fame  were attached to direct the grey man in  2015 per deadline however at the time  the brothers were reportedly overwhelmed  with their phase 3 projects for the mcu  and they opted to write the script for  the grey men but not direct as the movie  languished in development for several  more years the russo brothers were able  to hop back aboard as directors  officially in 2020. joe russo also took  a screenplay credit alongside avengers  endgame writer stephen mcfeely and  christopher marcus in a conversation  with fandango joe russo amped up the  movie saying i feel like the gray man is  basically everything we learned over the  last decade pour it into one film in the  last 10 years the russos have directed  some of the biggest movies ever made  including the final two avengers flicks  captain america the winter soldier and  captain america civil war it seems  likely that the grey man won't be  anything less than stellar  in july 2020 deadline exclusively  revealed that ryan gosling had joined  the grey man to play the titular  protagonist this marks the first major  motion picture for gosling since 2018  when he played neil armstrong in first  man speaking to empire about the grey  man gosling revealed that he wouldn't be  opposed to making some sequels saying  what i liked about this character is  that he wants something that most of us  want which is just to be free his goals  aren't monetary it's not about treasure  it's not revenge he just wants to have  the right to sit on the couch and watch  netflix like the rest of us during the  interview gosling revealed that six has  a dry sense of humor that'll be evident  in every scene you must be loyal what  gave it away the white pants the trash  dash  he might be known for playing the hero  but the grey man sees chris evans step  into the villain's shoes as six's  biggest adversary lloyd hansen director  joe russo even revealed that evans had  indicated being ready to take some  serious risks in his career which led  him to being cast as the antagonist  speaking to dead of geek russo explained  so it seemed obvious to us that the  right move here would be to offer chris  the sociopath and not the hero evans has  also teased what to expect from his  character telling empire in may 2022  he's a train wreck of a human being that  guy can be anything in any scene because  all he wants is anarchy i didn't kill  anybody in december 2020 deadline  revealed anna de armas had joined the  gray man as ci agent danny miranda the  armistice character is someone who takes  their job at the agency very seriously  she'll work closely with six but the duo  will spend some time figuring out if  they can be allies according to danny's  official poster for the film the agent  is untraceable suggesting she might be  able to help six escape lloyd's capture  not much else is known as de armas's  character as dany does not exist in the  gray man novel it's possible her  character is an amalgamation of others  from the book or inspired by one  specific character but the cast and crew  are keeping quiet for now  one of the later additions to the grey  man was burgerton's scene stealer reggae  jean-page the actor plays denny  carmichael a character pulled straight  from the book speaking to l page  revealed there's a lot of shadow and  contrast to this character it's  something that i don't think people have  seen a lot of from me specifically  before which was great fun for me to  play with denny is the head of cia  clandestine services so we can expect a  lot of mystery and sketchiness  surrounding the character the film marks  the first project for paige since his  shocking bridgeton exit the grey man  will prove if he's got what it takes to  make it on the big screen  billy bob thornton plays court gentry's  handler donald fitzroy in the grey man  netflix revealed that fitzroy recruited  gentry to join the sierra program and  he's recently been replaced as director  as one of the only allies six has left  fitzroy is in just as much danger from  what we know from the greyman novel  fitzroy will be used by lloyd hansen and  his allies to lure in six filling out  the grey man cast are a lot of  recognizable names oscar nominee alfree  woodard plays margaret cahill an old  friend of gentries who might be his last  resort in finding help outside the law  jessica hendwick stars as susannah  brewer who works alongside reggae  jean-page's denny carmichael indian  actor danush will play aviksan a deadly  assassin who targets six for an unknown  reason  there were many takeaways from the first  trailer for the great man the film seems  to be reminiscent of many action  franchises such as mission impossible  and james bond it looks like the movie  will be fast-paced but there will be  comedic relief from ryan gosling and  chris evans who have a few face-to-face  moments in the trailer the trailer  suggests that lloyd catches up with six  at least twice in the film with a fist  fight breaking out between the pair we  can also expect a car chase or two along  with gunfights explosions and extensive  stunt work anna de armas's danny miranda  and goslings 6 appeared together in the  trailer and it looks as though their  characters have come to trust one  another lloyd is as sociopathic as we  expected appearing to have no issues  killing people and with his sights laser  focused on 6. billy bob thornton's  donald fitzroy also gives the impression  that six is impossible to kill and might  be impossible to outwit  netflix is making history with the gray  man which is the platform's biggest  movie ever deadline reported that the  movie had a 200 million dollar budget  from the jump which puts it ahead of  former title holder red notice initially  the gal gadot film reportedly had a  budget of 160 million dollars but  constant delays from the covet 19  pandemic jumped the price to around 200  million dollars  the record held by the grey men seems to  be based on its initial budget and not  from add-ons along the way plus 200  million dollars is a far cry from  netflix's other big-budget films like  the irishman which cost 159 million  dollars six underground which came in at  150 million dollars and outlaw king  which cost 120 million dollars according  to joe russo a huge budget was essential  in order to make the grey man as  spectacular as any action movie that  would be released exclusively in  theaters russo even teased to empire the  viewers will feel that 200 million  dollars during the film's immense action  sequences  it seems pretty likely that netflix will  be making another the grey man movie  that was always the plan from the jump  with joe russo telling deadline in july  2020 the idea is to create a franchise  and build out a whole universe with ryan  at the center of it we have all  committed to the first movie and that's  gotta be great to get us to the second  movie there's also plenty of content to  pull from as mark granny's the grey man  series currently stands at 11 books  anthony russo also feels confident about  moving forward with the grey man  franchise telling the wall street  journal the grey man has a large  ensemble a layered story that you are  only seeing the tip of the iceberg we  have a lot of ideas about where to take  it next the only thing that might deter  a sequel is if the film fails to draw an  audience however with the russo brothers  at the helm and chris evans and ryan  gosling leading the charge it seems  likely that the grey man will be a clear  success  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  new netflix movies and tv shows are  coming soon subscribe to 